  "html": "<article id=\"post-6698\" class=\"container post-6698 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-uncategorized\">\n<div class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n<a href=\"/about-us/blog\" data-cta-gap=\"md\" data-cta-type=\"outline\" data-cta-content=\"mixed\" data-cta-minwidth=\"true\" class=\"cta\">\n    <svg class=\"icon cta-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-chevronleft\" /></svg><span >Blog Posts</span>\n\n</a></div>\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\t\t<h1 class=\"entry-title has-secondary-color mt-3\">Brown Friday: How to Avoid a Post-Thanksgiving Plumbing Nightmare</h1>\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-meta\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"posted-on p-sm\">Published on <span><time class=\"entry-date published\" datetime=\"2024-11-05T00:05:46+00:00\">November 5, 2024</time><time class=\"updated\" datetime=\"2025-04-12T01:38:52+00:00\">April 12, 2025</time></span></span>\t\t\t</div><!-- .entry-meta -->\n\t\t\t</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n\n\t\t\t<figure class=\"post-thumbnail\">\n\t\t\t\t<img width=\"900\" height=\"506\" src=\"/images/2024/11/featured-image-plumbing-russells-american-mechanical-services-brown-friday.webp\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" alt=\"Picture of a sink leaking heavily in a customer&#039;s house in Chesapeake, VA\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"/images/2024/11/featured-image-plumbing-russells-american-mechanical-services-brown-friday.webp 900w, /images/2024/11/featured-image-plumbing-russells-american-mechanical-services-brown-friday-300x169.webp 300w, /images/2024/11/featured-image-plumbing-russells-american-mechanical-services-brown-friday-768x432.webp 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1010px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 50vw, 768px\" title=\"Picture of a sink leaking heavily in a customer&#039;s house in Chesapeake, VA - Russell’s American Mechanical\" />\t\t\t</figure><!-- .post-thumbnail -->\n\n\t<div class=\"entry-content | asymmetric-container | mb-5\">\n\t\t<div class=\"asymmetric-main blog--main flow\">\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thanksgiving in Chesapeake, VA, is a time for gathering with family, enjoying delicious meals, and celebrating cherished traditions. However, the day after Thanksgiving, known in the plumbing industry as “Brown Friday,” brings a different challenge: it’s the busiest day of the year for plumbing service calls. With a surge in calls for clogged drains, malfunctioning garbage disposals, and overflowing toilets, Russell&#8217;s American Mechanical is well-acquainted with the post-holiday rush. While many shoppers are out searching for Black Friday deals, our skilled team is ready to respond to emergency plumbing situations across Chesapeake and nearby areas. But what makes Brown Friday so notorious, and how can you prevent a plumbing mishap? Let’s explore the reasons behind this trend and share practical tips to keep your home’s plumbing functioning smoothly.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What’s Behind the Name &#8220;Brown Friday&#8221;?</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The term “Brown Friday” is widely recognized in the plumbing industry due to the sharp increase in service calls after Thanksgiving. The reason for this surge is straightforward: the holiday’s extensive food preparation and increased guest traffic put extra strain on household plumbing. According to data from service platforms, calls for clogged drains, garbage disposal repairs, and toilet overflows often rise by over 50% on Brown Friday. Russell&#8217;s American Mechanical in Chesapeake has firsthand experience with how these holiday demands can challenge even the most reliable plumbing systems.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Issues often stem from food waste going down the drain, grease buildup, and the increased use of bathrooms by guests. These factors create the perfect storm that makes Brown Friday a challenging day for both homeowners and plumbers.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Does Thanksgiving Cause Plumbing Problems?</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thanksgiving puts significant stress on kitchens and bathrooms, resulting in common plumbing issues. Here’s why plumbing problems spike during this holiday:</p>\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n\n<li><strong>Overloaded Garbage Disposals</strong>: Disposals are built for convenience but aren’t designed to handle everything. Bones, fibrous foods, and grease can jam disposals, dull blades, or cause motor burnout, leading to clogs.<br></li>\n\n<li><strong>Clogged Kitchen Drains</strong>: Foods like mashed potatoes, gravies, and cooking oils can solidify as they cool, creating blockages that slow or stop drainage.<br></li>\n\n<li><strong>Overused Toilets</strong>: With more people in the house, toilets are used more frequently, increasing the risk of clogs, especially if guests flush items that shouldn’t go down the toilet.</li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Plumbing Data and Trends</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The reputation of Brown Friday as the busiest day for plumbers is backed by industry data. Reports show a clear increase in calls for drain cleaning, garbage disposal issues, and mainline stoppages right after Thanksgiving. Some plumbing companies report service requests increasing by as much as 20% compared to regular days. This trend underscores how Thanksgiving activities can place extraordinary demands on household plumbing. While the name “Brown Friday” may sound lighthearted, dealing with plumbing emergencies during a holiday weekend is anything but enjoyable.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tips to Avoid Brown Friday Plumbing Issues</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preventing a post-Thanksgiving plumbing issue is simpler than you might think. Follow these tips to protect your Chesapeake home’s plumbing system:</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. <strong>Be Selective About What Goes Down the Garbage Disposal</strong></h4>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Not everything should go down the disposal. Avoid fibrous foods, greasy leftovers, and bones. Run cold water while using the disposal to help move food particles through the pipes effectively.</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. <strong>Dispose of Grease Properly</strong></h4>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One common mistake is pouring grease down the drain. While liquid when hot, grease solidifies as it cools, creating clogs. Instead, let it cool in a container and dispose of it in the trash.</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. <strong>Use Drain Screens</strong></h4>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drain screens are simple tools that catch food particles and debris before they enter the pipes. Using them in your kitchen and bathroom sinks can prevent clogs and keep drains flowing smoothly.</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. <strong>Stagger Appliance Use</strong></h4>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Running the dishwasher, washing machine, and showers simultaneously can strain your plumbing system. Stagger these activities to prevent sudden pressure changes that can cause clogs or backups.</p>\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. <strong>Communicate Bathroom Etiquette</strong></h4>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It may feel awkward, but reminding guests to only flush toilet paper can save you from clogs. Even “flushable” items can cause plumbing issues. Providing a trash bin helps guests properly dispose of non-flushable items.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preparing for a Smooth Thanksgiving</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Brown Friday might be a known challenge for plumbers, but you can avoid it with a few simple precautions. By being mindful of what goes down the drain, properly disposing of grease, and spacing out appliance use, you can help your plumbing system handle holiday demands. If you do run into trouble, <a href=\"/\">Russell&#8217;s American Mechanical</a> is ready to assist Chesapeake residents with expert plumbing services. Wishing you a happy and stress-free Thanksgiving from all of us at Russell&#8217;s American Mechanical!</p>\n<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-left\">\n\t\t\t<img class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-image\" src=\"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac5b447183d176a95f013bbac6db80bfaf1d45c568f44676b19f7dc18387a2c?s=300&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g\" alt=\"author avatar\"/>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-right\">\n\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-header\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"author-name\">nearu</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-main\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"author-bio-link\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/author/nearu\">See Full Bio</a>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/author/nearu\" aria-label=\"See Full Bio\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\txmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\twidth=\"16\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\theight=\"17\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tviewBox=\"0 0 16 17\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfill=\"none\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<path\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\td=\"M5.52978 5.44L8.58312 8.5L5.52979 11.56L6.46979 12.5L10.4698 8.5L6.46978 4.5L5.52978 5.44Z\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t/>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</svg>\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-footer\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</div>\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"asymmetric-side blog--sidebar\">\n\t\t\t<div  class=\"card card--post has-white-background-color has-black-color\">\n        <div class=\"card__content\">\n                    <p class=\"card__content__title card__title h3\" title=\"Have a question?\" aria-label=\"Have a question?\">Have a question?</p>\n\n                    <div class=\"card__content__description card__description\"><div class=\"flow\"><p>Let’s connect and have a quick conversation to see how we can help.</p>\n<a href=\"tel:+17575254911\" aria-label=\"Call now: +17575254911\" dat